WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.416
- [Bart] Hello.
- Hey.

00:00:01.416 --> 00:00:04.917
- [Bart] I'm Bart, I practiced
my question so many times

00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:06.416
that I lost my voice.

00:00:06.416 --> 00:00:08.500
(audience laughter)

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.209
- That's amazing.

00:00:11.209 --> 00:00:14.292
- [Bart] First of all, I would
like to thank you because

00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:16.708
I started my career
as an entrepreneur by

00:00:16.708 --> 00:00:18.792
trying to build
the next Facebook.

00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:22.458
But thanks to your
speeches on self-awareness,

00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:26.125
I came to realize that I
lose sleep over borrowing

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:29.000
a hundred euros from my
brother so I probably will

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.083
never build the next Facebook.

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:33.042
Having that in mind.

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:35.792
So, a year ago,

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:40.416
I started to build a data
migration company, organically.

00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:43.209
So, I landed a
big customer, and now

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.375
I get paid every day,
and I'm developing my stuff.

00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:50.209
And we went live in
production in Chile,

00:00:50.209 --> 00:00:51.583
in December.

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:54.292
This year for the
same company we will do

00:00:54.292 --> 00:00:57.458
USA, Mexico and Canada.

00:00:57.458 --> 00:00:59.792
So it's growing really great.

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.209
But my question to you was,

00:01:01.209 --> 00:01:03.167
you talk a lot about patience,

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.917
but you also talk
sometimes about speed.

00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:08.083
And patience
for me that would be

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:09.792
continue with the same--

00:01:09.792 --> 00:01:11.261
- Can I answer you
real fast and you'll

00:01:11.261 --> 00:01:12.708
understand it forever?

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:13.666
- [Bart] Okay.

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:16.541
- Macro, patience. Micro, speed.

00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:19.042
- [Bart] Yeah. Okay.

00:01:19.042 --> 00:01:20.958
- And let me expand on it,
'cause that didn't work.

00:01:20.958 --> 00:01:21.833
Fuck.
(audience laughter)

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:25.458
No no, hold on, hold on, 
hold on, back back back.

00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:28.042
Macro patience.
You're a young man.

00:01:28.042 --> 00:01:30.125
Building something
meaningful, a relationship,

00:01:30.125 --> 00:01:33.625
a business, 
it takes 10, 20, 30 years.

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:36.750
On your day-to-day work,
you have to be fast.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.958
With the clients, they email
you, you email them back.

00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:41.334
Like, your day-to-day.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.708
But your vision?

00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:44.292
What you want
to achieve in life?

00:01:44.292 --> 00:01:46.541
You're not going to
build it in one year.

00:01:46.541 --> 00:01:49.458
And so many
people have it reversed.

00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:52.125
In the day-to-day, they're slow,

00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:54.958
and in the macro, they
want their business to be huge

00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:56.167
the next day.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:57.958
So you need to reverse it.

00:01:57.958 --> 00:02:02.167
- [Bart] So if you have to
make the decision between,

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:04.625
in my case,
building a better framework

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:08.209
or focusing on that, or
trying to find more customers,

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:10.666
what would you advise?

00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:13.625
Knowing that I don't need
the money of new customers

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:14.458
right now.

00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:15.792
- Both.
- [Bart] Okay.

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:18.625
(audience laughter)

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.125
- And so here's another,

00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:22.833
here's an answer of both:

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:25.375
Number one, how
hard are you working?

00:02:25.375 --> 00:02:26.125
I don't know.

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:29.042
If you're
working 12 hours a day,

00:02:29.042 --> 00:02:31.875
I feel like you could
work 17 if you want! Right?

00:02:31.875 --> 00:02:33.708
Number two, if
you're working every hour,

00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:35.541
and you can't work more,

00:02:35.541 --> 00:02:37.209
with the money that's coming in,

00:02:37.209 --> 00:02:39.792
too many young people
and too many young businesses

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.375
when they start
having money come in,

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:43.083
take it for themselves.

00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:44.583
They want to buy a good watch.

00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:45.958
They want to buy a good car.

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:47.917
They want to buy fancier shoes.

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.083
What I would do is,
when my first money,

00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:51.083
so here's my story.

00:02:51.083 --> 00:02:52.708
This is not advice
I'm giving just for fun.

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:53.583
This is my life.

00:02:53.583 --> 00:02:55.167
I walked in my dad's store,

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.541
it did $3 million a year,

00:02:56.541 --> 00:02:59.292
10 percent gross profit,
$300,000 dollars in profit

00:02:59.292 --> 00:03:00.625
before expenses,

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:02.958
we had no money,
I was making $40,000 a year,

00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:05.541
37,4, actually.

00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:08.375
And I built that
business from 3 to 45 million,

00:03:08.375 --> 00:03:10.292
in the first kind
of four or five years,

00:03:10.292 --> 00:03:11.500
and five years later,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.583
five years later this is doing
$45 million dollars in sales,

00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:17.167
and I'm making $40,000 dollars.

00:03:18.583 --> 00:03:19.875
This is the advice I gave.

00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:23.792
And by the way, I was
in my twenties, and a guy.

00:03:23.792 --> 00:03:26.583
The exact time, if you're
making that kind of money,

00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:29.541
that you want to use it
to do guy things.

00:03:29.541 --> 00:03:30.541
Right?

00:03:30.541 --> 00:03:31.917
I put it back into the business,

00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:33.875
I hired four more managers,
six more managers,

00:03:33.875 --> 00:03:36.250
seven more managers,
I did more advertising.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.583
I built a business.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:40.209
So if this money's coming from
Chile and U.S. and Mexico,

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:41.375
hire people.

00:03:41.375 --> 00:03:42.458
Then you can do both.

00:03:42.458 --> 00:03:43.792
- [Bart] Okay. Thanks.

00:03:43.792 --> 00:03:44.407
- You're welcome.

00:03:44.407 --> 00:03:49.008
(hip hop music)

